From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] init: do not override the verified boot and build properties

crDroid builds init with SPOOF_SAFETYNET=1 for every variant except eng.
SetSafetyNetProps() then sets ro.boot.verifiedbootstate=green,
ro.boot.flash.locked=1, ro.boot.veritymode=enforcing, ro.debuggable=0,
ro.secure=1, ro.adb.secure=1, ro.build.type=user,
ro.build.tags=release-keys, ro.crypto.state=encrypted and
ro.secureboot.lockstate=locked before the kernel command line is parsed.
These properties are read-only, so the values passed by the bootloader
and the values set by the build no longer take effect.

The Huawei MateBook E Go boots with an unlocked bootloader and an orange
verified boot state, and this build does not try to pass Play Integrity.
With the spoofed values the reported state contradicts the real one, and
adb remount refuses to run. Build init with SPOOF_SAFETYNET=0 for all
variants.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific policy]
---
 init/Android.bp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/init/Android.bp b/init/Android.bp
index 5a68ddb..bc8b725 100644
--- a/init/Android.bp
+++ b/init/Android.bp
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@ libinit_cc_defaults {
         "-DREBOOT_BOOTLOADER_ON_PANIC=0",
         "-DSHUTDOWN_ZERO_TIMEOUT=0",
         "-DWORLD_WRITABLE_KMSG=0",
-        "-DSPOOF_SAFETYNET=1",
+        "-DSPOOF_SAFETYNET=0",
         "-Wall",
         "-Werror",
         "-Wextra",
@@ -496,7 +496,7 @@ init_first_stage_cc_defaults {
         "-DSHUTDOWN_ZERO_TIMEOUT=0",
         "-DLOG_UEVENTS=0",
         "-DSEPOLICY_VERSION=30", // TODO(jiyong): externalize the version number
-        "-DSPOOF_SAFETYNET=1",
+        "-DSPOOF_SAFETYNET=0",
     ] + GLOBAL_HWASAN_OPTIONS,
 
     product_variables: {
